WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.520
In this video, I look at
common cookware materials—

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.480
aluminum, stainless steel,
and cast iron.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.334
Watch the video to find out
which might be best to use.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:17.032
"Are Aluminum, Stainless Steel,
Cast Iron, and Teflon Safe?"

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.160
Over the last decades, the toxicity
of aluminum for humans

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.240
has been heavily discussed and
is still not completely clarified.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.400
Those occupationally exposed
to aluminum in like smelter plants

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:37.240
suffer from oxidative stress, free
radicals, that can damage their DNA.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.560
But what about just using
aluminum cookware?

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.760
Articles like this, suggesting an
unrecognized public health risk,

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.680
was limited to the developing world
where cookware is made in informal shops

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.480
by casting liquid aluminum melted
from a collection of scrap metal,

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.840
including the likes of lead batteries,
which is how you can get

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.840
so much lead leaching into peoples' food.
But then this study was published

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:09.080
suggesting the aluminum
itself may be harmful.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.000
Most of our aluminum exposure comes
from processed junk that contains

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.440
aluminum-containing food additives,
including those within some processed

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.680
cheeses, baking powders, cake mixes,
frozen dough, and pancake mixes.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.240
But approximately 20% of the daily
intake of aluminum may come

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:31.120
from aluminum cooking utensils,
such as pans, pots, kettles, and trays.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.240
To see if this may be causing a problem,
they took blood from consumers

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.120
that used aluminum cookware
versus those that did not,

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.520
and found that not only were the
aluminum users walking around

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.640
with twice the level of
aluminum in their blood,

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.920
but they had more free radical damage
of their body fats and proteins.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.320
And the total antioxidant capacity of
their bloodstream was compromised,

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.240
so, no surprise, suffered
significantly more DNA damage.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.920
And indeed, those with the highest
levels of aluminum in their blood

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.560
tended to suffer significantly
more damage to their DNA.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:13.520
No surprise, since aluminum is
considered to be a pro-oxidant agent.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.640
These folks weren't just casually
using aluminum pots, though,

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.200
but specifically using them daily
to cook and store acidic foods,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.440
like yogurt and tomato sauce, which
can leach out more aluminum.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.720
But even just a week using like camping
dishes, which tend to be aluminum

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.920
since it's so light, if you were
incorporating something acidic,

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.880
like marinating a fresh catch in
lemon juice, could greatly exceed

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:46.960
the tolerable weekly intake
guidelines, especially for children.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.880
Once in a while is not going to make much
of a difference, but this suggests that

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:55.400
you may not want to be cooking
in aluminum day-in and day-out.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.040
What about aluminum drinking bottles?

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.800
They're nice and light but children
drinking two cups of tea or juice

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:07.480
a day from them could exceed the
tolerable aluminum exposure limit.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.480
So out of an abundance of
caution, safety authorities,

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.360
like the German Federal Institute
for Risk Assessment,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.000
recommend that consumers avoid
the use of aluminum pots or dishes

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:25.680
for acidic or salted foodstuffs such
as apple sauce, rhubarb, tomato puree,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:32.120
or salt herring to avoid any
unnecessary ingestion of aluminum.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.320
What about aluminum foil?

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.120
It's a common culinary practice to
wrap food in aluminum foil and bake it.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.760
The concern is that this
could potentially present

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.920
a hazardous source of
aluminum in the human diet.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:51.880
When put to the test, yes, there
was leakage from the foil to the food,

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:56.680
but the amount was so small that it would
be more of an issue for small children

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.680
or those suffering from
diminished kidney function.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.320
What about just wrapping of food
in foil to store in the fridge?

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:12.080
Only marginal increases in aluminum
are seen, unless the food is in contact

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.360
with both the foil and, at the same
time, certain other types of metal,

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.760
for example stainless steel,
which is largely iron.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:24.680
And so that sets up a battery and so
can lead to tremendous food aluminum

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.800
concentrations. For example, here
are the aluminum levels in a ham

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.640
before and after a day covered
in foil. But take that same ham

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:39.160
and that same day of foil on top
of a steel tray or serving plate,

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:43.160
and the aluminum levels
in the ham shoots up.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:47.000
And finally, you know how there's
sometimes a glossy side

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.640
of aluminum foil and then a dull side?
Which would be worse?

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:56.880
Fish fillets were baked and grilled
both ways, wrapped in the glossy side

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:04.600
versus wrapped in the dull side, and
no significant difference was found.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:08.480
In my last video I expressed concerns
about the use of aluminum cookware.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.080
So, what’s the best type
of pots and pans to use?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.280
Stainless steel is an excellent option,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.547
the metal chosen in applications where
safety and hygiene are considered

00:05:18.547 --> 00:05:21.360
to be of the utmost importance,
such as kitchenware.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.200
But what about studies showing
stainless steel can leach

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:27.560
nickel and chromium into
foods during cooking?

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:32.080
(That’s what keeps the iron in the
stainless steel unstained by rust.)

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.320
The leaching is really only
when they’re brand new.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.960
Metal leaching decreases with
sequential cooking cycles

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.960
and stabilizes after the
sixth time you cook with it.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.120
Under more common
day-to-day conditions,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.720
the use of stainless-steel pots
is considered to be safe

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:53.080
even for most people who are
acutely sensitive to those metals.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.840
A little leaching metal can be a good
thing in the case of straight iron,

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.360
like a cast iron skillet, which
can have the beneficial effect

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.680
of helping to improve iron status,
helping to potentially reduce

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.600
the incidence of iron deficiency anemia

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.480
among reproductive age
women and children.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:16.840
The only caveat is that you don’t
want to be frying in cast iron.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.480
Frying isn’t healthy regardless,
but at hot temperatures

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:25.480
vegetable oil can react with
the iron to create trans fats.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.080
What about using nonstick pans?

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.240
Teflon, also known as
polytetrafluoroethylene,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.000
is used as an inner coating
material in nonstick cookware.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:41.040
Teflon’s dark history was the subject
of a recent movie called Dark Waters,

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.640
starring Mark Ruffalo
and Anne Hathaway.

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:46.160
Employees in DuPont’s Teflon division

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.640
started giving birth to
deformed babies before DuPont

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.960
“removed all female staff” from the unit.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:58.960
Of course, they buried it all, hiding
it from regulators and the public.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.000
Despite this significant
history of industry knowledge

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.680
about how toxic some of the
chemicals used to make Teflon were,

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.680
they were able to keep it all hidden.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:13.520
But eventually they were forced to
settle for over half a billion dollars

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:17.040
after one of the chemicals was linked
to kidney and testicular cancers,

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:22.080
pregnancy-induced hypertension,
ulcerative colitis, and high cholesterol.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.240
“At normal cooking temperatures,
[Teflon]-coated cookware releases

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:31.560
various gases and chemicals that
present mild to severe toxicity.”

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:35.560
Here’s some of the different gases that
are released at different temperatures

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.960
and the toxic effects that
have been documented.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:42.040
You’ve heard of canaries in a coal mine?

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.480
They're more like canaries in the kitchen,

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:50.160
as cooking with Teflon cookware is well
known to kill pet birds in the house;

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:55.000
or Teflon coated heat lamp bulbs
wiping out half a chicken flock.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.160
“Apart from the gases released
during heating the cooking pans,

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.320
the coating itself starts
damaging after a certain period.

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:06.600
It's normally advised to use slow heating
when cooking in Teflon-coated pans,”

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:10.000
but you can imagine how
consumers might ignore that.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.280
And some of the Teflon can start
chipping off if you’re not careful

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:19.200
and make its way into the food, though
the effects of ingestion are unknown.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.000
This is the only study I could
find looking at the potential

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.840
human health effects of cooking
with nonstick pots and pans,

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.440
and the use of non-stick
cookware was associated with

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:32.680
about a 50 percent increased
risk of colorectal cancer.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.720
But that may be because
of what they were cooking.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.720
Non-stick cookware is used in
hazardous high-heat cooking methods,

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:45.000
like broiling, frying, grilling,
or barbecuing, mainly for meat,

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.640
poultry or fish, in which
carcinogenic heterocyclic amines

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:51.200
are formed from the animal protein.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.520
And then the animal fat can
produce another class of carcinogens

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:57.520
called polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:00.480
Though it’s possible it
was the Teflon itself,

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.680
which contains suspected carcinogens
like that C8 compound from the movie,

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:09.240
also known as PFOA,
perfluorooctanoic acid.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.840
“Due to toxicity concerns,
this chemical has been replaced

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:17.520
with other chemicals such as
GenX, but these new alternatives

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:21.600
are also suspected to
have similar toxicity.”

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:27.120
But we’ve already so contaminated the
Earth with it that we now can get it

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.440
prepackaged in food before it’s
even cooked, particularly in fish,

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.600
dairy products, and meat,
which is now the main source

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.240
of human exposure to
these toxic pollutants.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:44.480
Of those, seafood is the worst.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.760
In a study of diets from around the world,

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:51.960
fish and seafood were major contributors
of the perfluoroalkyl substances,

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:57.280
as expected, given that everything
eventually flows into the sea.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:00.800
Though the aquatic food chain
is the primary transfer mechanism

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:04.600
for these toxins into the human
diet, “food stored or prepared

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:08.240
in greaseproof packaging
materials,” like microwave popcorn,

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.520
may also be a source.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:15.080
And in 2019, Oral-B Glide
dental floss was tested.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.320
6 out of 18 dental floss products
they tested showed evidence

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.840
of Teflon-type compounds.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:21.840
Here’s the list.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.440
So, did those who used
those kinds of floss

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:27.320
end up with higher levels
in their blood stream?

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:29.120
Yes, apparently so.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:31.320
Higher levels of
perfluorohexanesulfonic acid

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:35.120
were found in Oral-B Glide flossers.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.200
There’s lots of environmental
exposures in the modern world

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.640
we can’t avoid, but we
shouldn’t be making things worse

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.680
by adding it to consumer products.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.400
But hey, at least it gives
us some power to lower

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:51.524
our personal exposure to
these harmful chemicals.

